{"name":"Fury","hex":"#ff0011","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Fury","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female personification of vengeance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Fury"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rage (emotion)","blocks":[{"text":"Rage is intense, uncontrolled anger that is an increased stage of hostile response to a perceived egregious injury or injustice."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Physiognomy.jpg/330px-Physiognomy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rage_(emotion)","wikidata":"Q153641"},{"title":"Nick Fury","blocks":[{"text":"Colonel Nicholas Joseph \"Nick\" Fury Sr. is a fictional character appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. Created by co-plotter/artist Jack Kirby and writer/editor Stan Lee, he first appeared in Sgt. Fury and his Howling Commandos #1, a World War II combat series that portrayed the cigar-chomping sergeant as leader of a U.S. Army Ranger unit."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/71/Nick_Fury_I.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nick_Fury","wikidata":"Q975100"},{"title":"Fury (2014 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Fury is a 2014 American war film written, directed, and co-produced by David Ayer. It stars Brad Pitt with Shia LaBeouf, Logan Lerman, Michael Peña, and Jon Bernthal as members of an American tank crew fighting in Nazi Germany during the final weeks of the European theater of World War II. Ayer was influenced by the service of military veterans in his family and by reading books such as Belton Y. Cooper's Death Traps, a 1998 memoir that underscores the high casualty rates suffered by American tank crews in combat against their better-equipped German counterparts."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/17/Fury_2014_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fury_(2014_film)","wikidata":"Q14786561"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/47-aspetti_di_vita_quotidiana%2Cira%2CTaccuino_Sanitatis%2C_Casana.jpg/500px-47-aspetti_di_vita_quotidiana%2Cira%2CTaccuino_Sanitatis%2C_Casana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/47-aspetti_di_vita_quotidiana%2Cira%2CTaccuino_Sanitatis%2C_Casana.jpg/500px-47-aspetti_di_vita_quotidiana%2Cira%2CTaccuino_Sanitatis%2C_Casana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rage, Tacuinum Sanitatis casanatensis (14th century).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A47-aspetti_di_vita_quotidiana%2Cira%2CTaccuino_Sanitatis%2C_Casana.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Rage-and-anger-fresco.jpg/500px-Rage-and-anger-fresco.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Rage-and-anger-fresco.jpg/500px-Rage-and-anger-fresco.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Angel with Temperance and Humility virtues versus Devil with Rage and Anger sins. A fresco from the 1717 Saint Nicholas church in Bukovets, Pernik Province, Bulgaria.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARage-and-anger-fresco.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/17/Sgt._Nick_Fury_Sr.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/17/Sgt._Nick_Fury_Sr.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Nick Fury as he initially depicted (prior to the loss of his eye) on the cover of Sgt. Fury and His Howling Commandos #12 (November 1964. Art by Jack Kirby.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASgt._Nick_Fury_Sr.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/14/NIck_Fury_%28Ultimate_Marvel_character%29.jpg/250px-NIck_Fury_%28Ultimate_Marvel_character%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/14/NIck_Fury_%28Ultimate_Marvel_character%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/14/NIck_Fury_%28Ultimate_Marvel_character%29.jpg/250px-NIck_Fury_%28Ultimate_Marvel_character%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Nick Fury in the alternate-universe imprint Ultimate Marvel.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANIck_Fury_(Ultimate_Marvel_character).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Tiger_131_%287527948486%29.jpg/500px-Tiger_131_%287527948486%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Tiger_131_%287527948486%29.jpg/1280px-Tiger_131_%287527948486%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Tiger_131_%287527948486%29.jpg/500px-Tiger_131_%287527948486%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tiger 131 – the only operating Tiger I tank in the world – was lent by The Tank Museum for the film. It is the first time a genuine Tiger I tank was used in a contemporary war film since 1950; 131 was restored to running condition between 1990 and 2003, and further work was only completed in 2012.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATiger_131_(7527948486).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/US_Sherman_%283666208242%29.jpg/500px-US_Sherman_%283666208242%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/US_Sherman_%283666208242%29.jpg/1280px-US_Sherman_%283666208242%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/US_Sherman_%283666208242%29.jpg/500px-US_Sherman_%283666208242%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Tank Museum's M4A2 76mm HVSS Sherman in 2009[14]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUS_Sherman_(3666208242).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Bundesarchiv_Bild_101I-635-3965-28%2C_Panzerfabrik_in_Deutschland.jpg/500px-Bundesarchiv_Bild_101I-635-3965-28%2C_Panzerfabrik_in_Deutschland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Bundesarchiv_Bild_101I-635-3965-28%2C_Panzerfabrik_in_Deutschland.jpg/500px-Bundesarchiv_Bild_101I-635-3965-28%2C_Panzerfabrik_in_Deutschland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Schachtellaufwerk wheel arrangement on a Tiger I, which is identical to that on the Tiger 131 used for the movie","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABundesarchiv_Bild_101I-635-3965-28%2C_Panzerfabrik_in_Deutschland.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Sherman_Mk.IIIAY_%E2%80%9CFury%E2%80%9D_%2844431847595%29.jpg/500px-Sherman_Mk.IIIAY_%E2%80%9CFury%E2%80%9D_%2844431847595%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Sherman_Mk.IIIAY_%E2%80%9CFury%E2%80%9D_%2844431847595%29.jpg/1280px-Sherman_Mk.IIIAY_%E2%80%9CFury%E2%80%9D_%2844431847595%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=